WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.740
Some cute and cuddly guests.&nbsp;
An unexpected onscreen attack.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:09.420
Keanu Reeves' first showbiz job&nbsp;
is a world away from "John Wick."

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:14.640
It's always fascinating to see the entertainment&nbsp;
exploits of big movie stars from before they were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:19.500
famous. There's Steve McQueen in "The Blob," a&nbsp;
low-budget horror movie that has almost nothing to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:24.000
do with the kinds of films McQueen would become&nbsp;
known for later in his career. Many who know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.440
Leonardo DiCaprio from his collaborations&nbsp;
with Martin Scorsese might be shocked to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:32.880
see him as part of the cast of family sitcom&nbsp;
"Growing Pains" in the early 90s. Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:37.020
Marylin Monroe was famously a pinup&nbsp;
girl before she broke into films,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:42.000
and there are several former child actors who have&nbsp;
managed to eclipse their young brushes with fame,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:47.160
such as Kurt Russell, who appeared opposite Elvis&nbsp;
Presley in "It Happened at the World's Fair."

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:51.480
When it comes to surprising early&nbsp;
roles, one of the most charming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:56.400
examples comes from the career of Keanu&nbsp;
Reeves. He's best known as the steely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:01.500
assassin John Wick and the messianic Neo&nbsp;
in "The Matrix," but once upon a time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:07.080
he was just another young person trying to make it&nbsp;
in the competitive world of Canadian broadcasting.

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:12.720
Back in 1984, a good five years before his&nbsp;
breakthrough in "Bill and Ted's Excellent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:16.800
Adventure," Reeves hadn't done any&nbsp;
real acting to speak of. The "Point&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:21.240
Break" star's first showbiz job was as a&nbsp;
correspondent on the Canadian Broadcasting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:26.820
Corporation's "Going Great," a youth-focused&nbsp;
news magazine program. One of his more unusual&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:31.680
assignments on the program has become&nbsp;
the stuff of pre-fame movie star lore.

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:37.500
Years before "Bill &amp; Ted's Bogus Journey," Keanu&nbsp;
Reeves was just another correspondent on "Going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:41.880
Great." His most memorable assignment&nbsp;
saw him covering the inaugural Canadian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:46.500
International Teddy Bear Convention, an event&nbsp;
that attracted serious teddy bear collectors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:51.960
from across the country and possibly the world.&nbsp;
As Reeves himself said during the assignment,

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:57.600
"When I was sent to check out the first&nbsp;
Canadian International Teddy Bear Convention,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:00.360
I thought I was in for a lot of craziness."

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:01.620
Reeves continued,

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:14.760
Luckily for fans of the future movie star, Reeves'&nbsp;
assignment covering the Canadian International&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:20.040
Teddy Bear Convention has made its way on to&nbsp;
YouTube. Many viewers have already noted that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:24.420
Reeves seemingly displays a hint of Ted Logan,&nbsp;
his character in the "Bill &amp; Ted" franchise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:29.460
in his approach to human interest TV news.&nbsp;
The "Destination Wedding" star manages to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:33.840
show an unbridled enthusiasm for the strange&nbsp;
world of teddy bear collecting. Basically,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:37.980
his report is a great reflection of&nbsp;
the open-heartedness he is known for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:42.780
when he's not killing rival assassins or rogue&nbsp;
agents in his most famous feature film roles.

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:46.132
"Why are all the bear's first name Teddy?"

00:02:46.132 --> 00:02:50.760
Of course, the violence of "John Wick" and&nbsp;
"The Matrix" isn't completely missing from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:54.660
Reeves' early brush with stardom. In&nbsp;
what has to be the video's highlight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.660 --> 00:03:00.840
Reeves performs a great gag where he pretends&nbsp;
to be attacked by one ostensibly friendly fluffy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:05.460
teddy bear. In this hilarious clip, he shows&nbsp;
an inkling of the incredible onscreen fighter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:09.720
he would one day become. Obviously, the moment&nbsp;
is also a great showcase of his sense of humor.

00:03:10.063 --> 00:03:11.863
"I've been looking all over for you."

00:03:11.863 --> 00:03:16.860
If you're a Reeves superfan, it's unlikely&nbsp;
that his "Going Great" coverage of the 1984&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:21.420
Canadian International Teddy Bear Convention&nbsp;
will replace "The Matrix" or "My Own Private&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:26.700
Idaho" in your personal Keanu Canon. However,&nbsp;
it undoubtedly provides an invaluable glimpse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:33.540
at the screen performer in his early days, and&nbsp;
may even be more entertaining than "47 Ronin."

